    "lawSection": "General Services, Commissioner of",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S8121A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto authorize the commissioner of general services to transfer and convey\ncertain unappropriated state land to the village of Freeport\n\nPURPOSE:\nThis legislation authorizes the commissioner of general\nservices to convey an abandoned state armory to the Village of Freeport\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection 1. authorizes the commissioner of\ngeneral services to transfer and convey State land located at 63\nBabylon Turnpike, Freeport, in the County of Nassau. This conveyance\nof Land Shall include a reverter of the land if the land ceases to be\nused for a police athletic center, educational opportunities,\ncultural activities, and related activities of the Village of Freeport.\n\nSection 2. Description of the parcel to be conveyed to the Village of\nFreeport\n\nSection 3. Description to be submitted to the Office of General Services\n\nSection 4. Application for land must be made within one year of the\neffective date\n\nSection 5. Effective date\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nAt the request of the Village of Freeport this\nlegislation would allow the Commissioner of General Services to\ntransfer the abandoned state armory to the Village of Freeport.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
